    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Type I: real conditions",
     "texto": [
      "In the **se** condition the present indicative (or future) is used, and in the consequence the present, future or imperative: **Se parti adesso, arriverai in tempo** (if you leave now, you will arrive on time); **Se hai tempo, chiama Anna** (if you have time, call Anna).",
      "It expresses everyday situations, general truths or direct instructions."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Negating the condition",
     "texto": [
      "To negate, **non** is added: **Se non piove, usciamo** (if it doesn't rain, we'll go out).",
      "The consequence can be an order: **Se piove, chiudi la finestra** (if it rains, close the window)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Condition (se + present)",
